IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `snap-core`
IMPORT `snap6-s2034`

-- TESTS for snap6-s2034.l4 (section 2034, Assistance for community food projects).
-- Every expected value is written here from the text quoted above the assertion, before the module was run.
-- JUST FALSE = "the text says no in its own words"; NOTHING = "not covered"; JUST TRUE = "the text says yes".

§ `Tests of section 2034`

§§ `(a)(1) community food project`
-- src:2984 | (1) Community food project
-- src:2985 | In this section, the term “community food project” means a community-based project that—
-- src:2986 | (A) requires a 1-time contribution of Federal assistance to become self-sustaining; and
-- src:2987 | (B) is designed—
-- src:2988 | (i)
-- src:2989 | (I) to meet the food needs of low-income individuals through food distribution, community outreach to assist in participation in Federally assisted nutrition programs, or improving access to food as part of a comprehensive service;
-- src:2990 | (II) to increase the self-reliance of communities in providing for the food needs of the communities; and
-- src:2991 | (III) to promote comprehensive responses to local food, food access, farm, and nutrition issues; or
-- the project fields, in order: community-based; 1-time contribution; (B)(i)(I) food needs; (B)(i)(II) self-reliance; (B)(i)(III) comprehensive responses; (B)(ii) specific needs.
-- community-based, 1-time, and all of (i)(I) to (III): a community food project.
#ASSERT `s 2034(a)(1) the project is a community food project` (`s 2034 project` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- src:2992 | (ii) to meet specific State, local, or neighborhood food and agricultural needs, including needs relating to—
-- src:2993 | (I) equipment necessary for the efficient operation of a project;
-- src:2994 | (II) planning for long-term solutions; or
-- src:2995 | (III) the creation of innovative marketing activities that mutually benefit agricultural producers and low-income consumers.
-- community-based, 1-time, and (B)(ii) alone: a community food project.
#ASSERT `s 2034(a)(1) the project is a community food project` (`s 2034 project` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (i)(I) and (II) without (III), and no (ii): not one ("(I) ...; (II) ...; and (III)").
#ASSERT `s 2034(a)(1) the project is a community food project` (`s 2034 project` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2034(a)(1) the project is a community food project` (`s 2034 project` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2034(a)(1) the project is a community food project` (`s 2034 project` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not community-based, or no 1-time contribution: not one.
#ASSERT `s 2034(a)(1) the project is a community food project` (`s 2034 project` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2034(a)(1) the project is a community food project` (`s 2034 project` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- src:2993 | (I) equipment necessary for the efficient operation of a project;
-- src:2994 | (II) planning for long-term solutions; or
-- src:2995 | (III) the creation of innovative marketing activities that mutually benefit agricultural producers and low-income consumers.
#ASSERT `s 2034(a)(1)(B)(ii) the need is one the text lists` `s 2034 equipment necessary for the efficient operation of a project` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2034(a)(1)(B)(ii) the need is one the text lists` `s 2034 planning for long-term solutions` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2034(a)(1)(B)(ii) the need is one the text lists` `s 2034 the creation of innovative marketing activities that mutually benefit agricultural producers and low-income consumers` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2034(a)(1)(B)(ii) the need is one the text lists` `s 2034 some other need` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `(a)(2) gleaner`
-- src:2997 | The term “gleaner” means an entity that—
-- src:2998 | (A) collects edible, surplus food that would be thrown away and distributes the food to agencies or nonprofit organizations that feed the hungry; or
-- src:2999 | (B) harvests for free distribution to the needy, or for donation to agencies or nonprofit organizations for ultimate distribution to the needy, an agricultural crop that has been donated by the owner of the crop.
-- the inputs, in order: collects surplus food; distributes it to hunger agencies; harvests a donated crop; for free distribution or donation to the needy.
#ASSERT `s 2034(a)(2) the entity is a gleaner` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2034(a)(2) the entity is a gleaner` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- collects but does not distribute to such agencies; harvests a donated crop but not for the needy: neither limb.
#ASSERT `s 2034(a)(2) the entity is a gleaner` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2034(a)(2) the entity is a gleaner` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2034(a)(2) the entity is a gleaner` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (A) and (B) are alternatives joined by "or": each on its own is enough, and mixing one half of each is not.
#ASSERT `s 2034(a)(2) the entity is a gleaner` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `(a)(3) hunger-free communities goal`
-- src:3001 | The term “hunger-free communities goal” means any of the 14 goals described in House Concurrent Resolution 302, 102nd Congress, agreed to October 5, 1992.
#ASSERT `s 2034(a)(3) the goal is a hunger-free communities goal` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2034(a)(3) the goal is a hunger-free communities goal` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2034(a)(3) the number of hunger-free communities goals` EQUALS 14

§§ `(b)(1) authority to make grants`
-- src:3004 | From amounts made available to carry out this chapter, the Secretary may make grants to assist eligible private nonprofit entities to establish and carry out community food projects.
#ASSERT `s 2034(b)(1) the Secretary may make a grant to assist the entity with the project` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2034(b)(1) the Secretary may make a grant to assist the entity with the project` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2034(b)(1) the Secretary may make a grant to assist the entity with the project` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2034(b)(1) the Secretary may make a grant to assist the entity with the project` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `(b)(2) limitation on grants`
-- src:3006 | The total amount of funds provided as grants under this section may not exceed—
-- src:3007 | (A) $1,000,000 for fiscal year 1996;
-- src:3008 | (B) $5,000,000 for each of fiscal years 2008 through 2014;
-- src:3009 | (C) $9,000,000 for each of fiscal years 2015 through 2018; and
-- src:3010 | (D) $5,000,000 for fiscal year 2019 and each fiscal year thereafter.
#ASSERT `s 2034(b)(2) the most that may be provided as grants in the fiscal year, in dollars` 1996 EQUALS JUST 1000000
-- fiscal years before 1996 and 1997 to 2007: in no subparagraph.
#ASSERT `s 2034(b)(2) the most that may be provided as grants in the fiscal year, in dollars` 1995 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2034(b)(2) the most that may be provided as grants in the fiscal year, in dollars` 1997 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2034(b)(2) the most that may be provided as grants in the fiscal year, in dollars` 2007 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (B) 2008 through 2014.
#ASSERT `s 2034(b)(2) the most that may be provided as grants in the fiscal year, in dollars` 2008 EQUALS JUST 5000000
#ASSERT `s 2034(b)(2) the most that may be provided as grants in the fiscal year, in dollars` 2014 EQUALS JUST 5000000
-- (C) 2015 through 2018.
#ASSERT `s 2034(b)(2) the most that may be provided as grants in the fiscal year, in dollars` 2015 EQUALS JUST 9000000
#ASSERT `s 2034(b)(2) the most that may be provided as grants in the fiscal year, in dollars` 2018 EQUALS JUST 9000000
-- (D) 2019 and each fiscal year thereafter.
#ASSERT `s 2034(b)(2) the most that may be provided as grants in the fiscal year, in dollars` 2019 EQUALS JUST 5000000
#ASSERT `s 2034(b)(2) the most that may be provided as grants in the fiscal year, in dollars` 2040 EQUALS JUST 5000000
-- the total against the limit: "may not exceed".
#ASSERT `s 2034(b)(2) the total provided as grants is within the limit` 2010 5000000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2034(b)(2) the total provided as grants is within the limit` 2010 5000001 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2034(b)(2) the total provided as grants is within the limit` 2016 9000000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2034(b)(2) the total provided as grants is within the limit` 2016 9000001 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2034(b)(2) the total provided as grants is within the limit` 1996 1000000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2034(b)(2) the total provided as grants is within the limit` 2001 1 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `(c) eligible entities`
-- src:3012 | To be eligible for a grant under subsection (b), a public food program service provider, a tribal organization, or a private nonprofit entity, including gleaners, must—
-- src:3013 | (1) have experience in the area of—
-- src:3014 | (A) community food work, particularly concerning small and medium-sized farms, including the provision of food to people in low-income communities and the development of new markets in low-income communities for agricultural producers;
-- src:3015 | (B) job training and business development activities for food-related activities in low-income communities; or
-- src:3016 | (C) efforts to reduce food insecurity in the community, including food distribution, improving access to services, or coordinating services and programs;
-- src:3017 | (2) demonstrate competency to implement a project, provide fiscal accountability, collect data, and prepare reports and other necessary documentation;
-- src:3018 | (3) demonstrate a willingness to share information with researchers, practitioners, and other interested parties; and
-- src:3019 | (4) collaborate with 1 or more local partner organizations to achieve at least 1 hunger-free communities goal.
-- the inputs, in order: kind of entity; experience (community food work, job training, food insecurity); competency; willingness to share; partners; goals.
#ASSERT `s 2034(c) the entity is eligible for a grant under subsection (b)` `s 2034 a public food program service provider` (`s 2034 experience` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) TRUE TRUE 1 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2034(c) the entity is eligible for a grant under subsection (b)` `s 2034 a tribal organization` (`s 2034 experience` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE) TRUE TRUE 2 3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2034(c) the entity is eligible for a grant under subsection (b)` `s 2034 a private nonprofit entity` (`s 2034 experience` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE) TRUE TRUE 1 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2034(c) the entity is eligible for a grant under subsection (b)` `s 2034 a gleaner` (`s 2034 experience` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) TRUE TRUE 1 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- each requirement missing in turn: (1) no experience, (2) no competency, (3) no willingness, (4) no partners, (4) no goal.
#ASSERT `s 2034(c) the entity is eligible for a grant under subsection (b)` `s 2034 a private nonprofit entity` (`s 2034 experience` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) TRUE TRUE 1 1 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2034(c) the entity is eligible for a grant under subsection (b)` `s 2034 a private nonprofit entity` (`s 2034 experience` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) FALSE TRUE 1 1 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2034(c) the entity is eligible for a grant under subsection (b)` `s 2034 a private nonprofit entity` (`s 2034 experience` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) TRUE FALSE 1 1 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2034(c) the entity is eligible for a grant under subsection (b)` `s 2034 a private nonprofit entity` (`s 2034 experience` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) TRUE TRUE 0 1 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2034(c) the entity is eligible for a grant under subsection (b)` `s 2034 a private nonprofit entity` (`s 2034 experience` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) TRUE TRUE 1 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a kind of entity (c) does not name: not covered, however well it satisfies (1) to (4).
#ASSERT `s 2034(c) the entity is eligible for a grant under subsection (b)` `s 2034 some other kind of entity` (`s 2034 experience` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) TRUE TRUE 5 5 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `(d) preference`
-- src:3021 | In selecting community food projects to receive assistance under subsection (b), the Secretary shall give a preference to projects designed to—
-- src:3022 | (1) develop linkages between 2 or more sectors of the food system;
-- src:3023 | (2) support the development of entrepreneurial projects;
-- src:3024 | (3) develop innovative linkages between the for-profit and nonprofit food sectors;
-- src:3025 | (4) encourage long-term planning activities, and multisystem, interagency approaches with multistakeholder collaborations, that build the long-term capacity of communities to address the food and agricultural problems of the communities, such as food policy councils and food planning associations; or
-- src:3026 | (5) develop new resources and strategies to help reduce food insecurity in the community and prevent food insecurity in the future by—
-- src:3027 | (A) developing creative food resources;
-- src:3028 | (B) coordinating food services with park and recreation programs and other community-based outlets to reduce barriers to access; or
-- src:3029 | (C) creating nutrition education programs for at-risk populations to enhance food-purchasing and food-preparation skills and to heighten awareness of the connection between diet and health.
-- the five kinds of project, in order (1) to (5).
#ASSERT `s 2034(d) the Secretary shall give the project a preference` (`s 2034 preference facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2034(d) the Secretary shall give the project a preference` (`s 2034 preference facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2034(d) the Secretary shall give the project a preference` (`s 2034 preference facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2034(d) the Secretary shall give the project a preference` (`s 2034 preference facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2034(d) the Secretary shall give the project a preference` (`s 2034 preference facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2034(d) the Secretary shall give the project a preference` (`s 2034 preference facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `(e) matching funds`
-- src:3032 | The Federal share of the cost of establishing or carrying out a community food project that receives assistance under subsection (b) may not exceed 50 percent of the cost of the project during the term of the grant.
-- 50 percent of a 1,000 dollar project is 500: at the limit is within; above is not.
#ASSERT `s 2034(e)(1) the Federal share is within the limit` 1000 500 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2034(e)(1) the Federal share is within the limit` 1000 501 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2034(e)(1) the Federal share is within the limit` 1000 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2034(e)(1) the Federal share is within the limit` 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:3034 | In providing for the non-Federal share of the cost of carrying out a community food project, the entity receiving the grant shall provide for the share through a payment in cash or in kind, fairly evaluated, including facilities, equipment, or services.
#ASSERT `s 2034(e)(2) the contribution counts toward the non-Federal share` `s 2034 a payment in cash` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2034(e)(2) the contribution counts toward the non-Federal share` `s 2034 a payment in kind, fairly evaluated: facilities` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2034(e)(2) the contribution counts toward the non-Federal share` `s 2034 a payment in kind, fairly evaluated: equipment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2034(e)(2) the contribution counts toward the non-Federal share` `s 2034 a payment in kind, fairly evaluated: services` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2034(e)(2) the contribution counts toward the non-Federal share` `s 2034 some other contribution` EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:3036 | An entity may provide for the non-Federal share through State government, local government, or private sources.
#ASSERT `s 2034(e)(3) the entity may provide the non-Federal share through this source` `s 2034 State government` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2034(e)(3) the entity may provide the non-Federal share through this source` `s 2034 local government` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2034(e)(3) the entity may provide the non-Federal share through this source` `s 2034 private sources` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2034(e)(3) the entity may provide the non-Federal share through this source` `s 2034 some other source` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `(f) term of grant`
-- src:3039 | A community food project may be supported by only a single grant under subsection (b).
#ASSERT `s 2034(f)(1) the project may be supported by a grant under subsection (b)` 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2034(f)(1) the project may be supported by a grant under subsection (b)` 1 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2034(f)(1) the project may be supported by a grant under subsection (b)` 2 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- src:3041 | The term of a grant under subsection (b) may not exceed 5 years.
#ASSERT `s 2034(f)(2) the term of the grant is within the limit` 5 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2034(f)(2) the term of the grant is within the limit` 6 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2034(f)(2) the term of the grant is within the limit` 5.5 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2034(f)(2) the term of the grant is within the limit` 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `(h) reports to Congress`
-- src:3051 | Not later than September 30, 2014, and each year thereafter, the Secretary shall submit to Congress a report that describes each grant made under this section, including—
-- "Not later than September 30, 2014, and each year thereafter".
#ASSERT `s 2034(h) the date by which the report for the year is due` 2013 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2034(h) the date by which the report for the year is due` 2014 EQUALS JUST (Date 30 9 2014)
#ASSERT `s 2034(h) the date by which the report for the year is due` 2025 EQUALS JUST (Date 30 9 2025)
-- submitted on the day, a day late, never submitted before or after the due date, no report due.
#ASSERT `s 2034(h) the Secretary submitted the report for the year in time` 2014 (JUST (Date 30 9 2014)) (Date 1 1 2015) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2034(h) the Secretary submitted the report for the year in time` 2014 (JUST (Date 1 10 2014)) (Date 1 1 2015) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2034(h) the Secretary submitted the report for the year in time` 2014 NOTHING (Date 1 10 2014) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2034(h) the Secretary submitted the report for the year in time` 2014 NOTHING (Date 30 9 2014) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2034(h) the Secretary submitted the report for the year in time` 2013 (JUST (Date 1 1 2013)) (Date 1 1 2015) EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:3052 | (1) a description of any activity funded;
-- src:3053 | (2) the degree of success of each activity funded in achieving hunger-free community goals; and
-- src:3054 | (3) the degree of success in improving the long-term capacity of a community to address food and agriculture problems related to hunger or access to healthy food.
#ASSERT `s 2034(h)(1) to (3) the report describes what it shall include` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2034(h)(1) to (3) the report describes what it shall include` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2034(h)(1) to (3) the report describes what it shall include` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2034(h)(1) to (3) the report describes what it shall include` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `(g) regulative rules, run with #TRACE`
-- The stable binary does not let #ASSERT take a #TRACE outcome, so each trace states the outcome it should print.
-- src:3044 | In carrying out this section, the Secretary may provide technical assistance regarding community food projects, processes, and development to an entity seeking the assistance.
-- (g)(1): the Secretary provides technical assistance. Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 2034(g)(1) the Secretary's permission to provide technical assistance` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Secretary` DOES `s 2034 provide technical assistance regarding community food projects, processes, and development` AT 3
-- src:3047 | The Secretary may provide for the sharing of information concerning community food projects and issues among and between government, private for-profit and nonprofit groups, and the public through publications, conferences, and other appropriate forums.
-- (g)(2)(A): the Secretary provides for the sharing of information. Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 2034(g)(2)(A) the Secretary's permission to provide for the sharing of information` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Secretary` DOES `s 2034 provide for the sharing of information concerning community food projects among government, private groups and the public` AT 3
-- src:3049 | The Secretary may share information concerning community food projects with researchers, practitioners, and other interested parties.
-- (g)(2)(B): the Secretary shares information with researchers. Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 2034(g)(2)(B) the Secretary's permission to share information with researchers and others` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Secretary` DOES `s 2034 share information concerning community food projects with researchers, practitioners, and other interested parties` AT 3

